{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And I will meet.</b> When I fix an appointment for you to speak with you — that place I will fix for the appointment, where I will come to speak to you." "<b>And I will speak with you from above the cover.</b> And in another place it says ״וַיְדַבֵּר ה׳ אֵלָיו מֵאֹהֶל מוֹעֵד לֵאמֹר״ (Leviticus 1) — this is the Mishkan, outside the curtain. So two verses contradict each other. The third verse comes and decides between them: ״וּבְבֹא מֹשֶׁה אֶל אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד וַיִּשְׁמַע אֶת הַקּוֹל מִדַּבֵּר אֵלָיו מֵעַל הַכַּפֹּרֶת וגוֹ׳״ (Numbers 7). Moses would enter the Mishkan, and once he came within the entrance, a voice would descend from heaven to between the cherubim, and from there go out and be heard by Moses in the Tent of Meeting (Sifrei)." "<b>And all that I command you to the children of Israel.</b> This vav is superfluous and subordinate, and there are many like it in Scripture. And this is how it is resolved: ״And [that which] I will speak with you there — all that I command you to the children of Israel — is it.״"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:32.787241200Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}